the winter storm has lashed Spain  bringing whiteout snow conditions and  winds of more than 140 kilometres an  hour  Gloria triggered weather alerts across  the country with some saying it could be  the worst ocean storm here the century  sea waters been pouring into the embro  Delta one of Spain's most important  wetlands flooding thousands of hectares  of rice crops the local mayor said he'd  never seen anything like it  locals in Girona looked on nervously as  the anja River rose almost breaking its  banks yesterday city officials told us  that water could possibly enter our shop  so we put this yet to try to prevent  water getting in because it would be a  major disaster at one point two hundred  thousand people were without power and  tens of thousands of students out of  school as roads remained impassable  in Mariah snow plows were brought in and  drivers dug into the drifts to find  their cars we had to spend a couple of  days here we were supposed to leave  yesterday but we couldn't because  everything was covered in even more snow  than it is now some were forced to use  more unconventional methods to forge a  path the only thing I could think about  was this tray from the kitchen because  we are waiting for shovels we decided we  better use whatever we had at home and  improvise a little bit  this isn't snow even though it looks  like it it's sea foam flooding the  streets of the small town of tossa de  mar about a hundred kilometres up the  coast from Barcelona  the storms gale force winds smashed into  several seafront towns damaging shops  and restaurants some waves were a  record-breaking 13.5 meters high as they  slammed into the shore  Barcelona's famous beaches didn't escape  the storm but they still pulled the  crowds and while several people thought  the weather was worth documenting  scientists expect scenes like this to  become more common along this coast  because of climate change  Alexey Brian al-jazeera
 

